                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "02f9c14f-7c48-35ff-95da-c632353c87f2",
                        "entry_id": "1d70385f-cb64-39dd-aa10-64d3855cb236",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. оплодотворить, оплодотворять"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "233770e6-9db1-405d-a4d8-565c430b5a33",
                                "sense_id": "02f9c14f-7c48-35ff-95da-c632353c87f2",
                                "text": "Внутриутробный, или пренатальный, период начинается с момента оплодотворения женской яйцеклетки и заканчивается рождением ребенка; внеутробный, или постнатальный, ― с начала рождения до смерти."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8409d92-4dd7-3a43-9729-5aca1eba8b38",
                        "entry_id": "1d70385f-cb64-39dd-aa10-64d3855cb236",
                        "glosses": [
                            "биол. слияние мужской и женской половых клеток, в результате которого образуется живая клетка, способная развиться в новый организм"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eff86319-a3a0-4c4b-8708-1b5be92aea55",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d70385f-cb64-39dd-aa10-64d3855cb236",
                        "target_lang_word": "fecundation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fecundation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2545dc5c-58f4-335c-acd4-ac8cfafc84f9",
                                        "entry_id": "7aa5c7b3-0b2a-3fc1-b94c-3930e95836ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process whereby a new organism is produced by fertilization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "867d2ef7-d10c-4a01-9b68-943aa32d3c3e",
                                                "sense_id": "2545dc5c-58f4-335c-acd4-ac8cfafc84f9",
                                                "text": "The fact that in most lands the moon was originally a female deity has led many historians to dispute the superiority of the moon over the sun in ancient mythology. In putting forth this argument they overlook one important and significant factor: the existence of a matriarchate preceding the domination of woman by man. That such a condition was perfectly natural will be realized when it is remembered there was no recognition of the part played by the male in fecundation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73f3cf68-0f24-4081-aa55-48f5e35dcb3e",
                                                "sense_id": "2545dc5c-58f4-335c-acd4-ac8cfafc84f9",
                                                "text": "In Neolithic agricultural societies, the sacrificed male and his remains were transferred to the fields needing fecundation, and there the Great Mother becomes the soil receiving the fertilizing blood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d454bc68-00ff-45b0-b64f-14937667427b",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d70385f-cb64-39dd-aa10-64d3855cb236",
                        "target_lang_word": "impregnation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "impregnation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e240965-e405-30fc-9d63-8e83e02ba940",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b8b91f-c813-35d3-8e7c-26211bcc7a0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of making pregnant; fertilization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98df2a83-4c8e-3ff4-9f4c-d0d1ac7aceda",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b8b91f-c813-35d3-8e7c-26211bcc7a0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fact or process of imbuing or saturating with something; diffusion of some element, idea etc. through a medium or substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53e01e40-3b7f-3546-805c-b97b5a57a5b4",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b8b91f-c813-35d3-8e7c-26211bcc7a0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That with which anything is impregnated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3febc2f-e2ea-3d88-adc6-aa96ffbf2a35",
                                        "entry_id": "f2b8b91f-c813-35d3-8e7c-26211bcc7a0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ore deposit, with indefinite boundaries, consisting of rock impregnated with ore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a95cafa-b65a-47f1-b3d0-865124533ba4",
                                                "sense_id": "b3febc2f-e2ea-3d88-adc6-aa96ffbf2a35",
                                                "text": "Oil-shales are often the last relics of a former impregnation with petroleum; they are associated with phenomena—such as the intrusive asphaltites or manjacks—common to petroliferous regions, but in many cases the parent oilfields, the sources of the former impregnation, are things of the past."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49eb1402-e5a2-4a37-b021-8938233072d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d70385f-cb64-39dd-aa10-64d3855cb236",
                        "target_lang_word": "fertilization",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fertilization",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "290c3be5-de77-3652-8ee3-8fb11bca28b7",
                                        "entry_id": "9c5b2c9d-c491-3039-8b75-aeee4361722c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or process of rendering fertile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9599aa4b-645d-374c-97ad-6563ee5c0f99",
                                        "entry_id": "9c5b2c9d-c491-3039-8b75-aeee4361722c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of fecundating or impregnating the gametes of animals, plants, etc.; including the process by which in flowers the pollen renders the ovule fertile, an analogous process in flowerless plants, or the joining of sperm and egg in animals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8633b09-c9c0-4c4a-bb79-3f611ca5d97e",
                                                "sense_id": "9599aa4b-645d-374c-97ad-6563ee5c0f99",
                                                "text": "In plants, the ability to recognize self from nonself plays an important role in fertilization, because self-fertilization will result in less diverse offspring than fertilization with pollen from another individual."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cc9aba3-f242-3339-acc3-7d5843c07bc5",
                                        "entry_id": "9c5b2c9d-c491-3039-8b75-aeee4361722c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of applying fertilizer to soil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
